# Content-safe Shopify theme pushes

When adding or updating theme **code** (sections, snippets, assets, layout), preserve merchant content that already lives in the Theme Editor.

## Never push these unless the user explicitly asks to sync/overwrite editor content

- `config/settings_data.json` — theme settings + section instances/settings
- `templates/**/*.json` — page section order and per-section settings/blocks
- `sections/*-group.json` — header/footer group content

Pushing these resets images, text, padding, and section order merchants configured in the editor.

## Required push pattern for new features

1. Add/update only code files (`.liquid`, `.css`, `.js`, new assets).
2. Push with `--only` for those paths, plus `--nodelete`.
3. For the live theme, also use `--allow-live`.
4. Do **not** edit remote template JSON to insert the new section — merchants add it in the Theme Editor after the code is live.
5. Prefer loading new CSS/JS from the section itself so `layout/theme.liquid` changes are unnecessary when possible.

Example:

```bash
shopify theme push --theme <LIVE_THEME_ID> --allow-live --nodelete \
  --only sections/nf-lifestyle-carousel.liquid \
  --only assets/nf-lifestyle-carousel.css \
  --only assets/nf-lifestyle-carousel.js
```

## Wrong

```bash
# Full directory push — overwrites settings_data + templates
shopify theme push --theme <LIVE_THEME_ID> --allow-live
```

## After a safe code push

Tell the merchant to refresh the Theme Editor and **Add section** → pick the new section (e.g. "NF Lifestyle Carousel"). Their existing section content stays intact.
